        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long to let driveway dry before sealing after cleaning it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "After pressure washing or cleaning your driveway, wait a minimum of 24 hours before applying sealer — and ideally 48 hours. This ensures the pavement surface is completely dry, not just surface-dry. Moisture trapped under an asphalt or concrete surface can prevent proper sealer adhesion and cause the product to peel or bubble within weeks. If you cleaned on a cloudy day or temperatures were below 65°F, extend the wait to 48–72 hours. Run your hand across the surface in a shaded area — if it feels even slightly cool or damp, wait longer.",
